A||N||16||clubracr||Just bought an 87 turbo with 12.48 documented E.T.    Have questions.||||1||
Z||000000||clubracr||10-17-2001||07:42 PM||||Hello. I had an 85 GT back in the late 80s and just purchased an 87 GT with a turbo setup. I was wondering if anyone knows of this car. It's from the Penn-Jersey Fiero Club. It's maroon with silver skirts. Has a turbo, NOS, Holley TBI, Electromotive CD ignition-distributorless, intercooled, performance computer, a wild looking exhaust system, engine is 3.1, balanced and blueprinted with Wiseco forged pistons, Wolverine cam, and several more performace modifications. Has been published in Car Carft, Turbo, and was the cover car for an issue of the club magazine. If this car rings a bell with anyone I'd appreciate learning some of its history. It has ran a 12.48 quarter mile without NOS and puts out approx. 300 hp without the bottle. I'm just getting started with it but plan to fix up the cosmetics a little. The scoops (4 of them) have some nicks and scratches and the nose as well. I hope to get some pics of it ready so I can email to narrow down the origins of this car. Should be quite a ride!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hartz||10-17-2001||07:44 PM||||Well, I don't know much about the origins of the car, but congratulations!  Sounds like a really neat car.  Look forward to hearing more about it.<P>Take care,<BR>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>home.mindspring.com/~hartzfeld||||reg||10
