Z||000009||NOS3800||10-17-2001||10:41 PM||||Your in luck, I know about this car. I have the magazine with it in it. If its the same one that is. Ron Myers used to own it. It has everything you stated. Over the roof style snorkle scoops? Thats what this one has in the pic. Unfortunately the pic is Black and White.In the article, the fastest ET is 13.0. It states it was with a 50 shot of NOS and had 280 HP @4900 rpm. Numbers were obtained using a Monitor 200 Scan Tool, whatever that is. Remember the article is from 1992. Article can be found in Turbo and Hi-Tech Performance magazine. September 1992 issue. Great find!<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||10
Z||000010||clubracr||10-17-2001||11:15 PM||||I think you hit the nail on the head. I have a cardboard box of books, notes, papers, diskettes, and all sorts of stuff I'm going through. Ron Myers was the guy who did the majority, if not all, of the mods. And I did find the E.T. slip of 12.48. Of course the stories can't yet be confirmed. Yes it could have been on nitrous and maybe my hp #s are off. I'm going by the info of the last owner. Apparently he ran some kind of onboard pc thing because I have diskettes of quarter mile runs, test sessions, and all sorts of stuff I don't understand. I race an old Porsche 914 with points so this is new technology to me! It's back to the mountain of papers and notes for me. See ya.||||reg||1
Z||000011||grinthock||10-18-2001||09:35 AM||||Great find, sounds like you have a good car with alot of work done.  Hopefully, it hasn't been abused too much, watch that turbo!  Change the oil, have the car looked over, catch issues before they start.  You WILL have issues, as all cars do so stay alert on that!<P>12.8?  That may or may not have been on bottle.  The Fieroshop here has a 2.8 turbo intercooled and was running 13's.  Depends on the engine buildup!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Wannabe||10-18-2001||08:56 PM||||Sounds like a new number for fastest V6 too!||||reg||1
Z||000013||clubracr||10-18-2001||09:32 PM||||Well at least yesterday was a good day. After fixing a bad ground, replacing a bad relay, and putting a few vacuum lines where they were supposed to be and tightening down all the rubber hoses that were sucking air I could start it up and drive it. Took it on 2 test runs and the car ran really good. Drove it hard and it pulled like a rocket. Today I went out to start it and nothing. Just turns over and occasionally backfires through the pipes. Just like it did before I got it to run yesterday. Back to the drawing board when I get time. For now it goes on the back burner. Have to finish some work on the race car and then I'll try the Fiero again.||||reg||1
